                     <title ref="LIT0049IHA#s36IHA"/>
                     <incipit xml:lang="ar">
                        <locus target="#1v">-1v</locus>بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمَنِ الرَحيْمِ تَبَارَكَ الَّذِي بِيَدِهِ المُلْكُ وَهْوَ عَلَي كُلِ شَئٍ قَدِيْرٌ</incipit>
                     <explicit xml:lang="ar">
                        <locus target="#15v">-15v</locus>وَيْلٌ يَومَئِذٍ لِّلْمُكَذِّبِيْنَ فَبِأَيِّ حَدِيْثٍ بَعْدَهُ يُؤْمِنُوْنَ<note>حَدِيْثٍ (sic) instead of حَدِيْثِ</note>
                     </explicit>
                     <note>67:1-77:50. Elegant hand of a not always careful copyist, as we can see from a few deletions and corrections here and there, and from corrections in the margins by another hand. Fourteen lines a page. Title of suras rubricated. Catchwords. In the margins also, clarification (tawḍīḥ, using takbīr, 3v). The identification of the scribe is based on notes in ASH00276 (fol. 13r) and ASH00265 (fol. 1r).</note>
                     <note/>
